{
  "sourceLanguage" : "en",
  "strings" : {
    "#%lld on GitHub" : {
      "comment" : "Tooltip of an issue number at the end of a point in What’s New, like “#32 on GitHub”.",
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "GitHub 上的 #%lld"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "%@ %@" : {
      "comment" : "Joins two sentences, one after the other. Leave out the space if your language doesn't put one between sentences.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "%1$@ %2$@"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "%1$@%2$@"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "%@ %lld-bit" : {
      "comment" : "A certificate's public key on the certificate page of the site panel: its type, then its size in bits, like “RSA 2048-bit”.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "%1$@ %2$lld-bit"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "%1$@ %2$lld 位"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "%@ (%@)" : {
      "comment" : "A button's tooltip: its name, then its keyboard shortcut in parentheses, like “Reload (⌘R)”.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "%1$@ (%2$@)"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "%1$@（%2$@）"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "%@ (System)" : {
      "comment" : "The first choice of Translate pages into, in Settings › Translation: the Mac's language, by name.",
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "%@（系统）"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "%@ afternoon" : {
      "comment" : "Name of a History session that began in the last week. The placeholder is the weekday, like “Tuesday”.",
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "%@下午"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "%@ afternoon, %@" : {
      "comment" : "Name of an older History session: the weekday, then the date, like “Sunday afternoon, October 18”.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "%1$@ afternoon, %2$@"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "%2$@ %1$@下午"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "%@ and %@" : {
      "comment" : "Under a space's name in Settings › Spaces: its pinned tabs, then its open tabs, like “3 pinned tabs and 2 open tabs”.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "%1$@ and %2$@"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "%1$@和 %2$@"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "%@ at %lld%%" : {
      "comment" : "Beside Page Size among the developer tools above the page, while a page larger than the window is shown smaller to fit: its size, then how large it's shown, like “1440 × 900 at 72%”.",
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "%1$@，缩放至 %2$lld%%"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "%@ can be your search engine" : {
      "comment" : "Toast after adding an extension that gives a search engine. The name is the engine's, like ChatGPT.",
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "可以把 %@ 设为你的搜索引擎"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "%@ can’t be deleted yet" : {
      "comment" : "Title of the sheet shown instead of the one that deletes a profile, while an import or an extension is still going into that profile. The placeholder is the profile's name.",
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "暂时无法删除“%@”"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "%@ can’t hear this tab. Its sound is protected or can’t be reached." : {
      "comment" : "Toast when an extension asks to hear a tab whose sound Zigzag can't hand it (protected video, or sound it can't reach). The placeholder is the extension's name.",
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "%@ 无法收听这个标签页：它的声音受保护或无法获取。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "%@ can’t listen to this tab while %@ is. Turn %@ off for this tab, then try again." : {
      "comment" : "Toast when an extension asks to hear a tab another extension is already listening to; only one can at a time, as in Chrome. The first placeholder is the extension that asked, the other two the one listening, like Sound Booster.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "%1$@ can’t listen to this tab while %2$@ is. Turn %3$@ off for this tab, then try again."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "%1$@ 无法收听这个标签页，因为 %2$@ 正在使用。请先为这个标签页关闭 %3$@，再试一次。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "%@ evening" : {
      "comment" : "Name of a History session that began in the last week. The placeholder is the weekday, like “Tuesday”.",
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "%@晚上"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "%@ evening, %@" : {
      "comment" : "Name of an older History session: the weekday, then the date, like “Sunday afternoon, October 18”.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "%1$@ evening, %2$@"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "%2$@ %1$@晚上"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "%@ from %@" : {
      "comment" : "Under a download's name in the downloads panel: the file's size and the site it came from, like 9 MB from example.com.\nUnder the big number when an import finishes: what it counts, then a browser's name, like “passwords from Arc”.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "%1$@ from %2$@"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "%1$@，来自 %2$@"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "%@ has a primary password. Type it to bring its passwords over." : {
      "comment" : "Problem in the Import window. The placeholder is a browser's name, like Firefox; primary password is Firefox's own term.",
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "%@ 设置了主密码。输入主密码即可导入其中的密码。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "%@ is a development site" : {
      "comment" : "Toast after a site is put on the list in Settings › Developer. The site is a host, like localhost.",
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "%@ 已成为开发网站"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "%@ is blocking ads on YouTube." : {
      "comment" : "After the explanation under “Block ads and trackers” in Settings › Privacy, while an ad blocker extension (its name, like uBlock Origin Lite) handles YouTube instead of Zigzag.",
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "%@ 正在拦截 YouTube 上的广告。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "%@ is listening to this tab" : {
      "comment" : "Toast when an extension starts hearing a tab's sound. The placeholder is the extension's name.",
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "%@ 正在收听此标签页"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "%@ is no longer a development site" : {
      "comment" : "Toast after a site is taken off the list in Settings › Developer. The site is a host, like localhost.",
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "%@ 不再是开发网站"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "%@ is on %@, a profile with its own sign-ins and extensions. The page reloads there and keeps its back and forward history." : {
      "comment" : "Message of the sheet that asks before a tab moves to a space on another profile. First the space's name, then the profile's.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "%1$@ is on %2$@. The page reloads there, with that profile’s sign-ins and extensions, and keeps its back and forward history."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "“%1$@”位于个人资料“%2$@”，它有自己的登录状态和扩展。页面会在那里重新载入，并保留前进和后退记录。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "%@ is on %@, a profile with its own sign-ins and extensions. The pages reload there and keep their back and forward history." : {
      "comment" : "Message of the sheet that asks before several tabs move to a space on another profile. First the space's name, then the profile's.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "%1$@ is on %2$@. The pages reload there, with that profile’s sign-ins and extensions, and keep their back and forward history."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "“%1$@”位于个人资料“%2$@”，它有自己的登录状态和扩展。这些页面会在那里重新载入，并保留前进和后退记录。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "%@ is using this tab" : {
      "comment" : "On the bar over a tab an AI app is using through MCP. The placeholder is the app's name, as it gives it.",
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "%@ 正在使用此标签页"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "%@ isn’t a Safari export Zigzag can open. In Safari, choose File › Export Browsing Data, then choose the zip it makes." : {
      "comment" : "Problem in the Import window. The placeholder is the file's name; File › Export Browsing Data is Safari's own menu wording.",
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "“%@”不是 Zigzag 能打开的 Safari 导出文件。在 Safari 中，选取“文件 › 导出浏览数据”，然后选择它生成的 zip 文件。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "%@ isn’t a password export Zigzag recognizes. Export a CSV from your password manager or browser and choose it." : {
      "comment" : "Problem in the Import window. The placeholder is the chosen file's name.",
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "“%@”不是 Zigzag 能识别的密码导出文件。请从你的密码管理器或浏览器导出 CSV 文件，然后选择它。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "%@ keeps its %lld passwords in a newer format Zigzag can’t read yet. Export them from %@’s Passwords page as a CSV file, then choose it here." : {
      "comment" : "Problem in the Import window. The placeholders are a browser's name, like Firefox, and how many passwords it has.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "%1$@ keeps its %2$lld passwords in a newer format Zigzag can’t read yet. Export them from %3$@’s Passwords page as a CSV file, then choose it here."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "%1$@ 的 %2$lld 个密码使用了 Zigzag 暂时无法读取的新格式。请在 %3$@ 的“密码”页面将它们导出为 CSV 文件，然后在这里选择。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "%@ late night" : {
      "comment" : "Name of a History session that began in the last week. The placeholder is the weekday, like “Tuesday”. Between midnight and 5 AM.",
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "%@凌晨"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "%@ late night, %@" : {
      "comment" : "Name of an older History session: the weekday, then the date, like “Sunday afternoon, October 18”. Between midnight and 5 AM.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "%1$@ late night, %2$@"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "%2$@ %1$@凌晨"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "%@ may have changed or moved. Open it once, then try again." : {
      "comment" : "Message of the notice when an extension that comes inside an app can't install. The placeholder is the app, like StopTheMadness Pro.",
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "%@ 可能已更改或移动。请先打开它一次，然后再试一次。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "%@ morning" : {
      "comment" : "Name of a History session that began in the last week. The placeholder is the weekday, like “Tuesday”.",
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "%@上午"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "%@ morning, %@" : {
      "comment" : "Name of an older History session: the weekday, then the date, like “Sunday afternoon, October 18”.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "%1$@ morning, %2$@"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "%2$@ %1$@上午"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "%@ muted" : {
      "comment" : "Spoken by VoiceOver after a tab row's name, for one page of a split: that page's title, then that it's muted.",
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "%@，已静音"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "%@ needs its app" : {
      "comment" : "Title of the note shown from an extension's button when its companion app isn't installed. The placeholder is the extension's name.",
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "%@ 需要配套的 App"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "%@ night" : {
      "comment" : "Name of a History session that began in the last week. The placeholder is the weekday, like “Tuesday”.",
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "%@夜里"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "%@ night, %@" : {
      "comment" : "Name of an older History session: the weekday, then the date, like “Sunday afternoon, October 18”.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "%1$@ night, %2$@"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "%2$@ %1$@夜里"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "%@ of %@" : {
      "comment" : "Under a download's name in the downloads panel: how much has come of how much, like 3.7 MB of 9 MB.\nUnder a download's name in the downloads panel: how much has come of how much, the unit said once, like 3.7 of 9 MB.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "%1$@ of %2$@"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "%1$@ / %2$@"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "%@ on %@" : {
      "comment" : "Under an installed app in Settings › General with more than one profile: the site, then the profile it uses, like “github.com on Work”.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "%1$@ on %2$@"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "%1$@，个人资料“%2$@”"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "%@ paused: another tab is playing" : {
      "comment" : "Toast when an extension hearing a streamed tab (YouTube) pauses because another tab, a private window or a video in Picture in Picture has sound; it carries on when that stops. The placeholder is the extension's name.",
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "%@ 已暂停：另一个标签页正在播放声音"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "%@ playing audio" : {
      "comment" : "Spoken by VoiceOver after a tab row's name, for one page of a split: that page's title, then that it plays sound.",
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "%@，正在播放音频"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "%@ says" : {
      "comment" : "Title of a page's JavaScript alert, confirm or prompt sheet. The placeholder is the site's host name, or “This page”.",
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "%@ 提示"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "%@ side panel" : {
      "comment" : "What VoiceOver calls an extension's side panel. The placeholder is the extension's name.",
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "%@ 边栏面板"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "%@ stays pinned to its own page" : {
      "comment" : "Toast after closing a pinned tab that had wandered to another page. The title is the pinned tab's.",
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "“%@”会固定在它自己的页面上"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "%@ to %@" : {
      "comment" : "The time a session or a site's pages span on the History page, like “2:10 to 4:45 PM”.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "%1$@ to %2$@"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "%1$@ 至 %2$@"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "%@ wants more access" : {
      "comment" : "Title of the sheet shown when an extension asks for more access. The name is the extension's.\nTitle of the sheet shown when an extension's update asks for more access. The name is the extension's.",
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "%@ 请求更多权限"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "%@ works together with an app on your Mac, and Zigzag couldn’t find it. Install the app, then reopen Zigzag." : {
      "comment" : "Shown from an extension's button when its companion app isn't installed. The placeholder is the extension's name.",
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "%@ 需要配合 Mac 上的一个 App 使用，但 Zigzag 找不到它。请安装该 App，然后重新打开 Zigzag。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "%@ × %@" : {
      "comment" : "A page's size in points, width then height, like “393 × 852”.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "%1$@ × %2$@"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "%1$@ × %2$@"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "%@, %@" : {
      "comment" : "A size in the Page Size menu of the developer tools above the page: its name, then its width and height, like “iPhone, 393 × 852”.\nAccessibility label of the address in the sidebar on a plain http page: the site, then that it's not secure.\nOn the Permissions row of the site panel: how many allowed, then how many blocked, like “2 allowed, 1 blocked”.\nUnder a download's name in the downloads panel: how much has come, then the time left, like 3.7 of 9 MB, a minute left.\nVoiceOver name of a command bar result: its title, then what's under it.\nVoiceOver name of a download in the downloads panel: the file's name, then what's under it.\nWhat VoiceOver says for a row in the Passwords window: the site, then the username.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "%1$@, %2$@"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "%1$@，%2$@"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "%@, %lld percent color" : {
      "comment" : "VoiceOver, in the space editor's color wheel: a knob's color family, then how much color, like “Blue, 40 percent color”.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "%1$@, %2$lld percent color"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "%1$@，色彩 %2$lld%%"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "%@, current space" : {
      "comment" : "Spoken by VoiceOver as the space switcher's choice moves to the space you're in. The placeholder is its name.",
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "%@，当前空间"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "%@, folder, %lld pinned" : {
      "comment" : "Accessibility label of a folder in the sidebar: its name, then how many pinned tabs it holds.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
